# score: Marcha de Cádiz — «Los cornetas nos anuncian» (Chueca & Valverde, 1886)
# summary: 200 bars / 9 voices / 3:27
# tempo: 116
# time: 2/4
# key: Bb
# bars: 200
# pack: instrument.json
# master: rms=-13

# text @b1: Final del Acto I de la zarzuela «Cádiz», Teatro Apolo, Madrid,
# text @b1: 20 de noviembre de 1886. Fue himno nacional de facto una década.
# text @b1: The opening fanfare uses only the natural harmonics a bugle can
# text @b1: sound — Bb F Bb D F Bb — because that is what a corneta is.
# text @b2: FORM and idiom are faithful. The NOTES are not: no score was
# text @b2: reachable, so the copla and estribillo are written to the shape of
# text @b2: the sung text, not transcribed. The bugle calls are constrained by
# text @b2: physics and are probably close.
# text @b3: Las cornetas son un pájaro. El platillo es un coche que pasaba.

# instruments:
#   c1 = corneta I (treble, voice=bright, send=0.20, gain=-3)
#   c2 = corneta II (treble, voice=bright, s=2, send=0.20, gain=-7)
#   me = melodía (treble, voice=call, send=0.18, gain=-2)
#   hi = flautín (treble, voice=glide, send=0.24, gain=-13)
#   ha = armonía (treble, voice=mid, send=0.16, gain=-13)
#   ba = bajo (bass, voice=buzz, lpf=1100, send=0.05, gain=-6)
#   sn = caja (perc, voice=tick, hpf=1700, rel=0.02, send=0.12, gain=-9)
#   bd = bombo (perc, voice=buzz, st=-28->-46, curve=exp, tau=0.04, lpf=200, rel=0.10, send=0.04, gain=-4)
#   cy = platillo (perc, voice=car, send=0.34, gain=-9)


